\DOC MEMSAFE_ARITH_TAC

\TYPE {MEMSAFE_ARITH_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a goal whose conclusion is an arithmetic statement by linear arithmetic
over the numeric assumptions of the goal.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal {A ?- t} where {t} is a natural-number
(in)equality, or a conjunction or disjunction of such, it selects the
arithmetic assumptions from {A}, builds the single implication from them to
{t}, and discharges it with an arithmetic decision procedure; non-arithmetic
assumptions (machine-state reads, list and event facts, quantified statements)
are discarded.
{
       A ?- t
     ==========  MEMSAFE_ARITH_TAC
      (no goals)
}

\FAILURE
Fails when {t} does not follow by linear arithmetic from the extracted
arithmetic assumptions, the underlying decision procedure reporting that no
contradiction can be derived. In the observed failures the conclusion asserts
containment relations between two independent address variables, the needed
facts being non-arithmetic assumptions about address regions rather than the
arithmetic ones used.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces it is applied to goals with large assumption lists
mixing arithmetic and non-arithmetic facts, with conclusions that are linear
bounds on sums and products of variables and constants.

\ENDDOC
